🌸 About My Prelim Activities

During the Prelim period, I completed three creative activities that allowed me to explore different aspects of visual communication and digital design.

Each activity helped me develop my understanding of how design principles, color, typography, and visual storytelling can work together to communicate ideas effectively.

My three activities were:

🎀 Activity 1 — Presentation Design Principles
🩷 Activity 2 — Color Palette and Typography
💌 Activity 3 — Social Media Infographics and Mini Project Documentation

The activities were developed step-by-step, allowing me to apply what I learned from one activity to the next.

🎀 ACTIVITY 01
📚 Presentation Design Principles

✨ Learning the foundations of good visual design. ✨

💗 What I Created

For Activity 1, I created a presentation focused on Design Principles. The presentation discussed important principles that can be used to make visual content more organized, balanced, and engaging.

The goal was not only to provide information but also to make the presentation itself demonstrate the design principles being discussed.

🌷 Why I Chose This Concept

I chose this concept because understanding design principles is an important first step in becoming a better designer.

Before creating more complex visual projects, I wanted to understand how elements such as balance, contrast, alignment, hierarchy, and repetition affect the way people view and understand information.

🎨 Design Principles I Applied

🎀 Balance

I arranged the elements on each slide so that the visual weight was distributed properly. This helped prevent the slides from looking too crowded on one side.

💗 Contrast

I used differences in color, size, and weight to make important information stand out. This helped guide the viewer's attention to the most important parts of each slide.

✨ Alignment

I kept text and visual elements aligned consistently. This made the presentation look cleaner and more organized.

🌸 Proximity

Related information was placed close together, while unrelated information was separated. This made the content easier to understand.

👑 Hierarchy

I used different font sizes, weights, and placements to show which information was most important.

🎀 Repetition

I repeated certain colors, fonts, and design elements throughout the presentation to create consistency.

💕 How These Principles Improved My Presentation

Applying these principles helped transform my presentation from a simple collection of information into a more organized and visually engaging presentation.

The principles helped me create a clear visual flow and made it easier for viewers to follow the information from one slide to another.

🛠️ My Creative Process

01 → Plan
I identified the main information and organized the topics.

02 → Sketch
I planned the layout and placement of text and visual elements.

03 → Design
I applied design principles to each slide.

04 → Review
I checked the consistency, readability, spacing, and overall appearance.

05 → Finalize
I made adjustments and completed the final presentation.

🩷 ACTIVITY 02
🎨 Color Palette and Typography

💅 Giving my designs their personality.

💗 What I Created

For Activity 2, I created a Color Palette and Typography study. This activity allowed me to explore how colors and fonts can work together to create a specific mood and visual identity.

I experimented with different combinations and selected colors and typefaces that matched the style I wanted to achieve.

🌸 Why I Chose This Concept

I wanted to understand how design choices can communicate emotions without using words.

For my concept, I wanted something that felt soft, feminine, playful, and creative, which inspired me to use a girly-pop aesthetic.

🎀 My Color Palette

My color palette focused mainly on pink and soft pastel tones.

💗 Color	🎀 Purpose
🌸 Soft Pink	Creates a gentle and feminine feeling
🩷 Light Pink	Adds softness and visual harmony
💕 Bright Pink	Adds energy and emphasis
🤍 White	Keeps the design clean and balanced
✨ Light Pastels	Adds a soft and playful aesthetic

I chose these colors because they represent the mood I wanted my design to communicate: fun, youthful, creative, and feminine.

✍🏻 Typography

For typography, I used a combination of fonts with different visual characteristics.

I selected:

🎀 A decorative or script-style font for special headings
💗 A clean font for body text
👑 Bold typography for important information

The purpose of combining these styles was to create contrast and hierarchy while keeping the design readable.

✨ Why I Selected These Fonts

I wanted my typography to match the personality of my color palette.

The decorative font adds personality and makes the design feel more playful, while the simpler font keeps the information easy to read.

This combination allowed me to balance creativity and readability.

💕 My Creative Process

01 → Inspiration
I looked at different visual styles and identified the aesthetic I wanted.

02 → Color Exploration
I experimented with different shades and combinations.

03 → Font Selection
I tested different typefaces and compared their appearance.

04 → Combination
I combined the colors and fonts to see how they worked together.

05 → Final Selection
I selected the palette and typography combination that best represented my concept.

💌 ACTIVITY 03
📱 Social Media Infographics & Mini Project Documentation

✨ Putting everything together and turning information into visuals. ✨

💗 What I Created

